    "description": [
      "Accelerator mass spectrometry (AMS) was used to obtain",
      "Typically, the extracted CO",
      "and a stable isotope measurement was performed using the same instrument used in the original analyses (Roeloffzen et al., 1991).",
      "Then, the CO",
      "Individual standard samples were graphitized along with the corresponding atmospheric CO",
      "The",
      "http://www.c14dating.com/agecalc.html.",
      "More information about sample preparation and analysis at the Groningen AMS can be found at: http://www.rug.nl/ees/onderzoek/programmas/radiocarbonams/sampleTreatmentAms The primary literature reference for the material presented here is Meijer et al. (2006).",
      "The statistical analysis included curve fitting described by Cleveland (1979). A seasonal pattern was then fit to the residuals, and the data are given in terms of these trends and departures from them."
